cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use NoiseVault, cite this software and give the fingerprint of every device profile
  you used (nv cite <profile> prints it).
title: "NoiseVault"
abstract: >-
  NoiseVault pins the calibrated noise of a real quantum device on a date as one small file, a
  profile, and turns it into a working noise model for Qiskit, Cirq, PennyLane or Stim, with a
  report of what each simulator reproduces exactly or approximates. Profiles carry provenance,
  license and a SHA-256 fingerprint of their physics, so a simulation can be tied to the exact
  calibration it used.
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-01
authors:
  - family-names: "Goyal"
    given-names: "Dev D."
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dvgyl/noisevault"
url: "https://github.com/dvgyl/noisevault"
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - noise model
  - device calibration
  - reproducibility
  - qiskit
  - cirq
  - pennylane
  - stim
